                            <comment id="16127530" author="ilyak" created="Tue, 15 Aug 2017 17:01:19 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;I&apos;m afraid we can&apos;t use solution 1).&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;We can mind the lifecycle of Ignite we&apos;ve got or started, but JDBC driver can&apos;t make sure Ignite that was already existing, and now shared, isn&apos;t closed while still being needed by JDBC.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;2) should probably be implemented, with appended UUID as in loadConfiguration() method but in more generic way.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
                            <comment id="16129007" author="githubbot" created="Wed, 16 Aug 2017 16:11:26 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;GitHub user alamar opened a pull request:&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/2460&quot; class=&quot;external-link&quot; target=&quot;_blank&quot; rel=&quot;nofollow noopener&quot;&gt;https://github.com/apache/ignite/pull/2460&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    &lt;a href=&quot;https://issues.apache.org/jira/browse/IGNITE-5790&quot; title=&quot;Xml config can not be used in jdbs and user code simultaneously&quot; class=&quot;issue-link&quot; data-issue-key=&quot;IGNITE-5790&quot;&gt;&lt;del&gt;IGNITE-5790&lt;/del&gt;&lt;/a&gt; SQL: Append UUID to names of Ignite instances opened by JDBC&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    All Ignite instances created by Jdbc driver should now be either named or appended with ignite-jdbc-driver-UUID to avoid conflicting with instances created in other places.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;    Had to inline parts of IgnitionEx.start() to apply changes to every decision branch.&lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;You can merge this pull request into a Git repository by running:&lt;/p&gt;

